Video operator registry (src/video-ops)

src/video-ops/ holds one descriptor module per video filter. The code in it was
moved, not rewritten, from modules whose provenance is recorded in NOTICE and in
src/activation/NOTICE.activation. Those notices still apply to the moved code:
- formats.ts: the negotiation table, pixel-format loss scoring, chooseFormat and
  the union-find merge formerly copied in video-format-negotiation.ts,
  video-graph-formats.ts and activation/formats.ts (libavfilter/formats.c,
  avfiltergraph.c, libavutil/pixdesc.c).
- null.ts, format.ts, scale.ts, transpose.ts, negate.ts, options.ts: scoped option
  parsing formerly in video-parse.ts (libavfilter/avfilter.c, graphparser.c,
  vf_format.c, vf_scale.c, vf_transpose.c, vf_negate.c), and the timed scale,
  flip enable= and AV_OPT_TYPE_BOOL parsing formerly in activation/resolver.ts
  (vf_scale.c, libavutil/opt.c).
- split.ts, nullsink.ts, stack-options.ts, hstack.ts, vstack.ts: frame-graph pad
  parsing formerly in video-graph-resolver.ts (split.c, vsink_nullsink.c,
  vf_stack.c).
- crop.ts, aspect-options.ts, setsar.ts, setdar.ts, setpts.ts: activation option
  parsing and configured geometry formerly in activation/resolver.ts and
  activation/formats.ts (vf_crop.c, vf_aspect.c, setpts.c).
- descriptor.ts and registry.ts: the per-path descriptor contract and registry
  validation. They contain no FFmpeg code.
